    "result_text": "The build passes with the single acceptance test green, and the audit log confirms the new identity format (`customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\nHere's a summary of what I implemented for the owner-identity redesign:\n\n**New `customerCode` format `<REGION>-<HASH8>`**\n- `CustomerCodeGenerator.generate(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)` now builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. Sequence numbers are gone entirely. It also gained `regionOf(customerCode)` to read the REGION segment back out.\n\n**Region derivation single-sourced**\n- Extracted `RegionResolver` (model) \u2014 postcode-range first, city-table fallback, then `UNKNOWN`. This was previously inline in `Owner.getLocality()` and is now shared by both the identity and the locality.\n\n**Everything downstream moved to the new identity**\n- **Controller** (`addOwner`): resolves region via `RegionResolver`, passes the already-normalized telephone + last name to the generator. Removed the now-dead `CityOwnerCounter` dependency (still used by `CityOwnerCapacityValidator`, so the class stays).\n- **Membership number** and **check digit** are built from `customerCode`, so they follow the new value with no code change.\n- **Audit record** logs `customerCode`, so it now records the region/hash identity.\n- **`Owner.getLocality()`** now returns the REGION segment of the `customerCode` (falling back to `RegionResolver` only when no code has been assigned yet, e.g. seed data), so locality is genuinely a function of the identity.\n\n**Reuse / structure**\n- Extracted a shared `Sha256.hex(...)` utility and refactored `HouseholdKey` to use it instead of its private copy \u2014 no duplicated hashing logic.\n- Updated stale javadocs and the OpenAPI descriptions for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality`.",
